er benign or malignant. The characteristics of these nodules are assessed to evaluate the risk of cancer. Their management is guided by the American Thyroid Association, ensuring that appropriate monitoring or treatment is provided based on the specific circumstances of each case. Overall, thyroid nodules may require careful observation or intervention depending on their nature and associated risks.", "THYROID CANCER:Thyroid cancer is a type of cancer that occurs in the thyroid gland, which can be predicted through ultrasound features of thyroid nodules.", "MICROCALCIFICATIONS:Microcalcifications are small deposits of calcium in the thyroid nodules that are associated with a higher risk of malignancy.", "MARGINS IRREGULARES:Irregular margins of thyroid nodules are a characteristic that indicates a higher risk of malignancy.", "HIPOECOGENICIDAD:Hypoechogenicity refers to the appearance of thyroid nodules on ultrasound, which can be associated with malignancy.", "ANALYSIS:Analysis refers to the systematic review and evaluation of thyroid nodules and their characteristics in relation to cancer risk.", "PAAF:PAAF, or Punción Aspiración con Aguja Fina, is a medical procedure utilized for diagnostic purposes. It is primarily employed to evaluate thyroid nodules and assess the potential for malignancy. Additionally, PAAF is also performed to obtain tissue samples from liver lesions, aiding in the diagnosis of various conditions. This technique is significant in the medical field for its role in determining the nature of suspicious lesions in both the thyroid and liver.", "CATEGORÍA BETHESDA:El sistema Bethesda es una clasificación de hallazgos citológicos en PAAF de nódulos tiroideos que categoriza el riesgo de malignidad.", "VANDERPAS J.:Vanderpas J. es un autor que ha escrito sobre epidemiología nutricional y metabolismo de hormonas tiroideas.", "BALOCH ZW:Baloch ZW es un autor que ha contribuido a la terminología diagnóstica y criterios morfológicos para el diagnóstico citológico de lesiones tiroideas.", "HAUGEN BR:Haugen BR is a prominent author who has significantly contributed to the field of thyroid health, particularly in the development of management guidelines for thyroid conditions. He is recognized as one of the authors of the American Thyroid Association Management Guidelines for Adult Patients with Thyroid Nodules and Differentiated Thyroid Cancer, specifically the 2015 edition. His work focuses on providing comprehensive guidance for the management of thyroid nodules and differentiated thyroid cancer, reflecting his expertise and commitment to improving patient care in this area."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}